      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the rewrite. i think the \"ripple effect\" part is nice. \n\nit's still looking a bit thin on that specific keyword count though. i just checked and the score is still pretty marginal. i know i've said this before, but i really don't want it to look like we're just playing the system, but if we don't hit a certain density of those core concepts—sustainability, empowerment, resilience, etc.—the automated filter might just toss the whole proposal before a human even reads it.\n\ncan we do one last pass? maybe make it a bit more robust. try to really drive home those specific themes of being able to scale the project, making it transformative for the whole region, and ensuring the impact is resilient over time. just keep it grounded in the real-world stuff so it doesn't feel like empty fluff, okay? we just need to make sure those core pillars are very clearly and strongly represented in the text.",
